{"title": "Inside Colonel Clucks: how we raise broilers in Jos", "seo_title": "About Colonel Clucks Poultry: Broiler Farm in Jos, Plateau State", "description": "Meet Colonel Clucks Poultry, a small broiler farm in Jos. See Batch 1 facts, our daily routine, feed plan, growth targets and how birds get from our farm to your table.", "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"lead\"} -->\n<p class=\"lead\">A small farm, a daily routine and a lot of records. Here is how we raise our Batch 1 broilers in Jos, Plateau State, from the 5:30am torch-lit check to the evening lock-down.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"byline\"} -->\n<p class=\"byline\">Written by the <strong>Colonel Clucks team</strong>, Jos, Plateau State · Updated 21 November 2026</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"answer\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group answer\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tag\"} -->\n<p class=\"tag\">Batch 1 at a glance</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Our flock, as of 21 November 2026</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Fact</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Birds</th><td>50 broilers</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Hatched</th><td>About 28 October 2026</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">On our farm since</th><td>13 November 2026</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Age on 21 November</th><td>About 24 days (3 and a half weeks)</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Birds alive on 21 November</th><td>All 50</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Sale window</th><td>18 to 23 December 2026, when the birds are about 7 weeks old</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Target weight on sale days</th><td>3 to 3.5 kg per bird</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Products</th><td>Whole or cut birds</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Location</th><td>Jos, Plateau State</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Partner</th><td>Longon Farms Nigeria Limited</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Batch 1 facts</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tnote\"} -->\n<p class=\"tnote\">We update this table as the batch grows.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"toc\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group toc\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"toc-title\"} -->\n<p class=\"toc-title\">On this page</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#who\">Who we are</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#day\">A day on the farm</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#feed\">What the birds eat and drink</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#growth\">How we track growth</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#home\">Housing and comfort</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#health\">Health and records</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#table\">From our farm to your table</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#partner\">Our partner</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#faq\">Questions</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">About us</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"who\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"who\">Who we are</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Colonel Clucks Poultry is a small, farm-raised agric start-up in Jos, Plateau State. Batch 1 is 50 broilers, which means every order gets a personal reply from us and not a form letter.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We are growing in public. That means we share what we do each day, the numbers we keep and the things we are still learning, on this page and on our <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/colonelclucks/\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a>, <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61596370718430\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> and <a href=\"https://x.com/ColonelClucks\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a> pages. If you are planning your Christmas table, our <a href=\"/christmas-chicken-jos/\">pre-order page</a> and <a href=\"/chicken-size-guide/\">size guide</a> will help.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Routine</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"day\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"day\">A day on the farm</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Broilers grow fast and they grow while they eat, so we check them four times a day and top up feed and water late at night. Most of our work is looking, listening and keeping things clean.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>Check</th><th>What we do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">5:30am</th><td>Morning check (the most important)</td><td>Take a torch, because it is still dark until about 6:30. Look before touching anything: healthy birds are active, spread out and noisy. Remove any dead birds and write down the number. Note whether feed or water ran out overnight. Wash and refill the drinkers. Top up feed so feeders are about two-thirds full. Keep the sides mostly closed until the chill lifts.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">12:00pm</th><td>Midday check</td><td>Top up water and feed. Birds drink most in the warm afternoon. Turn wet or caked litter, especially around drinkers. Sniff the air: a strong ammonia smell means we need more airflow or drier litter.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">4:00pm</th><td>Afternoon check</td><td>Top up water and feed. Walk slowly through the flock and watch for limping, sleepy birds, runny droppings or a bird sitting alone. Film a short clip for our social pages.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">6:30pm</th><td>Evening lock-down</td><td>Fill the feeders to the top for the night. Fill the drinkers. Close the sides against the cold Jos night but leave a small gap at the top for air. Switch on the light, with about an hour of dark. Check doors against dogs, cats and rats.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">7:30pm</th><td>Records</td><td>Log the day: deaths, feed used, water used and how the flock looks.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">9:00 to 10:00pm</th><td>Late top-up</td><td>A quick feed and water top-up so nothing runs dry before morning.</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Our daily checks</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Nutrition</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"feed\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"feed\">What the birds eat and drink</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Broilers move through three feeds as they grow: starter, grower and finisher. We change feeds gradually, mixing the new feed in over about three days. We never ration. If the feeders run empty, we give more.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Dates</th><th>Feed</th><th>Feed per day</th><th>Water per day</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">15 to 18 Nov</th><td>Starter</td><td>About 4 kg</td><td>About 8 litres</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">19 to 26 Nov</th><td>Grower (mixed in over 3 days)</td><td>About 5 to 6 kg</td><td>About 10 to 12 litres</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">27 Nov to 2 Dec</th><td>Grower</td><td>About 7 to 8 kg</td><td>About 15 litres</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">3 to 9 Dec</th><td>Finisher</td><td>About 9 kg</td><td>About 18 litres</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">10 to 16 Dec</th><td>Finisher</td><td>About 10 kg</td><td>About 20 litres</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">17 to 23 Dec</th><td>Finisher</td><td>About 11 kg</td><td>About 22 litres</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Our feed and water guide for all 50 birds</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tnote\"} -->\n<p class=\"tnote\">Guide numbers for 50 birds. We follow the feed supplier's own age guide if it differs. In the first weeks the birds sometimes finished all their feed and water overnight, which is why we fill feeders to the top at night and have added extra feeders.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Growth</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"growth\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"growth\">How we track growth</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Every Monday we weigh 5 random birds and log the average. That tells us early if the flock is falling behind. If it is more than about 0.2 kg behind, we check feed, water and cold nights first.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Monday</th><th>Age</th><th>Target average weight</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">16 Nov</th><td>19 days (2.7 weeks)</td><td>About 0.7 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">23 Nov</th><td>26 days (3.7 weeks)</td><td>About 1.1 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">30 Nov</th><td>33 days (4.7 weeks)</td><td>About 1.6 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">7 Dec</th><td>40 days (5.7 weeks)</td><td>About 2.2 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">14 Dec</th><td>47 days (6.7 weeks)</td><td>About 2.8 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">21 Dec</th><td>54 days (7.7 weeks)</td><td>3 to 3.5 kg (sale window)</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Our Monday weigh-in targets</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tnote\"} -->\n<p class=\"tnote\">Guide figures for well-managed broilers, trimmed a little for local conditions. They are targets, not results. We will post our real weigh-ins on our social pages.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Housing</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"home\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"home\">Housing and comfort</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Covered house.</strong> Our birds live in a covered house with ventilation we adjust through the day and night. We do not describe them as free range.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Cool Jos nights.</strong> We close the sides at night but always leave a small gap at the top so fresh air can get in.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Light.</strong> The light stays on overnight with about an hour of dark.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Dry litter.</strong> We turn wet litter every day and replace soaked litter completely. Wet litter and ammonia are early warning signs of trouble.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Clean water.</strong> Drinkers are washed and refilled every morning, and deep-cleaned every Friday along with the feeders.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Security.</strong> Doors are checked every evening against dogs, cats and rats.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Health</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"health\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"health\">Health and records</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We write everything down. Each day we log deaths, feed used, water used and whether the flock looks healthy, and we keep a health calendar for vitamins and any vaccines or treatments. Records are how we spot a problem on day one and not day five.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Warning sign</th><th>What we do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">More than 1 bird dies in a day</th><td>Call the vet the same day</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Several birds gasping, sneezing or with swollen eyes or heads</th><td>Call the vet the same day</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Green or bloody droppings</th><td>Call the vet the same day</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Birds suddenly stop eating or drinking</th><td>Call the vet the same day</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">When we call the vet the same day</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"callout\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group callout\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"callout-title\"} -->\n<p class=\"callout-title\"><strong>What we do not claim</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We have not applied for organic or other certification labels, so we do not use those words about our birds. What we can show you is our daily routine, our records and photos and video from the farm.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Sale days</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"table\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"table\">From our farm to your table</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>When</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Now</th><td>Pre-orders open on our <a href=\"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/#order\">order form</a>. First come, first served.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">15 to 17 December</th><td>We confirm every order by WhatsApp and agree pickup or delivery times.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">18 to 23 December</th><td>Birds are prepared fresh each morning, weighed, labelled with weight, date and farm name, and kept chilled.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Sale days</th><td>You collect from the farm in Jos, or we deliver within Jos. Orders go with a care card for storage and cooking.</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Batch 1 timeline</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"note\"} -->\n<p class=\"note\">Read the full details on our <a href=\"/christmas-chicken-jos/\">Christmas chicken page</a>, or work out your size with the <a href=\"/chicken-size-guide/\">size guide</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Partner</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"partner\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"partner\">Our partner</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"partner\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group partner\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{IMG_LONGON}}_ID,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"className\":\"partner-logo\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full partner-logo\"><img src=\"{{IMG_LONGON}}_URL\" alt=\"Longon Farms Nigeria Limited logo\" class=\"wp-image-{{IMG_LONGON}}_ID\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"ptext\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group ptext\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"peyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"peyebrow\">Official partner</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In collaboration with <strong>Longon Farms Nigeria Limited</strong></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"contact\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group contact\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Location:</strong> Jos, Plateau State</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>WhatsApp:</strong> <a href=\"https://wa.me/2349135556086\" rel=\"noopener\">+234 913 555 6086</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:cluckscolonel@gmail.com\">cluckscolonel@gmail.com</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">FAQ</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"faq\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"faq\">Questions</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Where is the farm?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In Jos, Plateau State. We share the pickup details when we confirm your order.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Is this your first batch?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Yes. Batch 1 is 50 broilers, which is why we are sharing the process openly.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>How old are the birds when you sell them?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>About 7 weeks, from 18 to 23 December 2026.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Are your birds free range?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>No. They live in a covered house with ventilation we adjust through the day and night, so we do not describe them as free range.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Can I follow the flock's progress?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Yes. We post short clips and updates on <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/colonelclucks/\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a>, <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61596370718430\" rel=\"noopener\">Facebook</a> and <a href=\"https://x.com/ColonelClucks\" rel=\"noopener\">X</a>, and you can join the flock newsletter on our <a href=\"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/#newsletter\">main site</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>What do you sell?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Whole birds and cut birds, prepared fresh on the sale day. See the <a href=\"/christmas-chicken-jos/\">Christmas chicken page</a> for sizes and how to order.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"disclose\"} -->\n<p class=\"disclose\"><strong>Who wrote this:</strong> the Colonel Clucks team, from our own daily routine and records. Dates, ages and numbers are current as of the update date and we change them as the batch grows.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Keep reading</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">More from the farm</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"related\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group related\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"rel\"} -->\n<p class=\"rel\"><a href=\"/christmas-chicken-jos/\"><strong>Christmas chicken in Jos</strong></a><br>Sizes, pickup, delivery and how to pre-order.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"rel\"} -->\n<p class=\"rel\"><a href=\"/chicken-size-guide/\"><strong>How much chicken per person?</strong></a><br>A calculator, portion tables and cooking times.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"ctaband\",\"align\":\"full\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group ctaband alignfull\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{IMG_HAPPY}}_ID,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"className\":\"cta-mascot\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full cta-mascot\"><img src=\"{{IMG_HAPPY}}_URL\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-{{IMG_HAPPY}}_ID\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Want to taste the difference?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Batch 1 is ready 18 to 23 December 2026. Pre-order whole or cut birds today.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:buttons {\"className\":\"cc-btns\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons cc-btns\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"btn-gold\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button btn-gold\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/#order\">Place your order</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button -->\n<!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"btn-line\",\"linkTarget\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer noopener\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button btn-line\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://wa.me/2349135556086?text=Hello%20Colonel%20Clucks%2C%20I%20have%20a%20question%20about%20ordering%20chicken.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Ask on WhatsApp</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"Article\", \"headline\": \"Inside Colonel Clucks: how we raise broilers in Jos\", \"description\": \"Meet Colonel Clucks Poultry, a small broiler farm in Jos. See Batch 1 facts, our daily routine, feed plan, growth targets and how birds get from our farm to your table.\", \"datePublished\": \"2026-11-21\", \"dateModified\": \"2026-11-21\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/about-the-farm.html\", \"image\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/logo.png\", \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Colonel Clucks Poultry\", \"url\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/\"}, \"publisher\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Colonel Clucks Poultry\", \"logo\": {\"@type\": \"ImageObject\", \"url\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/logo.png\"}}}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Our farm\", \"item\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/about-the-farm.html\"}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"LocalBusiness\", \"name\": \"Colonel Clucks Poultry\", \"url\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/\", \"image\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/logo.png\", \"description\": \"Farm-raised broiler start-up in Jos, Plateau State, selling whole or cut chicken.\", \"email\": \"cluckscolonel@gmail.com\", \"telephone\": \"+2349135556086\", \"address\": {\"@type\": \"PostalAddress\", \"addressLocality\": \"Jos\", \"addressRegion\": \"Plateau State\", \"addressCountry\": \"NG\"}, \"sameAs\": [\"https://www.instagram.com/colonelclucks/\", \"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61596370718430\", \"https://x.com/ColonelClucks\"]}</script>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "slug": "about-the-farm"}